+---
+id: dl-004-importtasks-reports-per-line-rejections-and-never-throws
+type: decision-log
+title: "importTasks reports per-line rejections and never throws"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+Bulk import must cope with bad lines in spreadsheet data without losing the good ones.
+
+## Decision
+`importTasks` never throws and does not stop at the first bad line: each line is added through `list.add`;
+failures (invalid input, duplicates, a line with more than three fields) are reported as `{ line, reason }`
+with the original line number. A title containing `;` is therefore rejected, not guessed at.
+Lines with fewer fields (e.g. just a title) are accepted.
+
+## Consequences
+Valid lines are imported even when others fail; a duplicate title inside the text is rejected like any duplicate.
